    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "A magnet has an invisible pull. It can pull some metal things without even touching them!",
      "punch": "invisible",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🧲",
        "text": "An invisible pull!",
        "cue": "invisible",
        "sub": "No touching needed",
        "sub_cue": "touching"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Does it pull every kind of metal?"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Nope! Magnets pull things made with iron, like paper clips and nails. They don't pull wood or plastic.",
      "board": {
        "type": "checklist",
        "title": "Will it stick?",
        "icon": "🧲",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Paper clip",
            "icon": "📎",
            "cue": "paper",
            "ok": true
          },
          {
            "text": "Nails",
            "icon": "🔩",
            "cue": "nails",
            "ok": true
          },
          {
            "text": "Wooden block",
            "icon": "🪵",
            "cue": "wood",
            "ok": false
          },
          {
            "text": "Plastic cup",
            "icon": "🥤",
            "cue": "plastic",
            "ok": false
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Why does iron stick, but wood doesn't?"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Iron is full of teeny tiny magnet bits, all pointing every which way. A magnet lines them up, so they pull together!",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "Inside iron",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": "Tiny magnet bits",
            "icon": "✨",
            "cue": "tiny"
          },
          {
            "label": "Pointing every way",
            "icon": "🔀",
            "cue": "pointing"
          },
          {
            "label": "Magnet lines them up",
            "icon": "➡️",
            "cue": "lines"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Do magnets ever push instead of pull?"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Yes! Every magnet has two ends, called north and south. North and south pull together, but two norths push apart!",
      "punch": "push",
      "board": {
        "type": "compare",
        "left": {
          "label": "Opposites",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "North + South",
              "icon": "🧲",
              "cue": "together"
            }
          ]
        },
        "right": {
          "label": "Same ends",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "North + North",
              "icon": "↔️",
              "cue": "push"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Whoa! Is anything else a magnet?"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "The whole Earth is like a giant magnet! That's why a compass needle always points north.",
      "board": {
        "type": "gallery",
